===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsɛɹəˈtəʊnɪn/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsɛɹəˈtoʊnɪn/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-serotonin.wav|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|neurotransmitter}} An [[indoleamine]] [[neurotransmitter]], [[5-hydroxytryptamine]], that is involved in [[depression]], [[appetite]], etc., and is crucial in maintaining a sense of [[well-being]], [[security]], etc.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-08-21|author=|title=Generation of a Tph2 Conditional Knockout Mouse Line for Time- and Tissue-Specific Depletion of Brain Serotonin|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0136422|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0136422|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=Notably, mouse lines targeting genes codifying for '''serotonin''' receptors, for enzymes involved in 5-HT synthesis as Tph1 and Tph2, in its metabolism as monoaminoxidase A (MAOA) or in its re-uptake as '''serotonin''' transporter (SERT), have been generated.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kristen Rogers|title=If antidepressants are killing your sex life, here’s what you can do|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/03/21/health/antidepressants-sexual-side-effects-tips-wellness/index.html|date=2024-03-21|passage=The class of antidepressants most commonly associated with sexual dysfunction is selective '''serotonin''' reuptake inhibitors, or SSRIs, which treat depression by ultimately increasing levels of the neurotransmitter '''serotonin''' in the brain.}}

